[ti:A Lost Ship]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.23]Lesson 32 | 第32课
[00:02.18]A lost ship | 一艘沉船
[00:09.03]Did the crew of the Elkor find what they were looking for? Why? | “埃尔科”号的船员找到他们要找的东西了吗？为什么？
[00:15.38]The salvage operation had been a complete failure. | 打捞作业彻底失败了。
[00:19.20]The small ship, Elkor, which had been searching the Barents Sea for weeks, was on its way home. | 小船“埃尔科”号在巴伦支海搜寻了数周之后，正在返航途中。
[00:26.72]A radio message from the mainland had been received by the ship's captain instructing him to give up the search. | 船长收到大陆发来的无线电报，指示他放弃搜寻。
[00:34.53]The captain knew that another attempt would be made later, | 船长知道日后还会再作尝试，
[00:38.10]for the sunken ship he was trying to find had been carrying a precious cargo of gold bullion. | 因为他试图寻找的沉船上装载着贵重的金锭。
[00:45.33]Despite the message, the captain of the Elkor decided to try once more. | 尽管接到电报，埃尔科号船长仍决定再试一次。
[00:51.89]The sea bed was scoured with powerful nets and there was tremendous excitement on board when a chest was raised from the bottom. | 他们用结实的渔网在海底拖曳，当一只箱子从海底捞上来时，船上的人都激动万分。
[01:00.76]Though the crew were at first under the impression that the lost ship had been found, | 起初船员们以为找到的就是那艘沉船，
[01:05.99]the contents of the chest proved them wrong. | 但箱内的东西证明他们错了。
[01:09.52]What they had in fact found was a ship which had been sunk many years before. | 他们实际上找到的是一艘多年前沉没的船。
[01:15.62]The chest contained the personal belongings of a seaman, Alan Fielding. | 箱子里装有水手艾伦·菲尔丁的私人物品。
[01:20.76]There were books, clothing and photographs, together with letters which the seaman had once received from his wife. | 其中有书籍、衣服、照片，还有这位水手从前收到的妻子的信件。
[01:28.34]The captain of the Elkor ordered his men to salvage as much as possible from the wreck. | 埃尔科号船长命令船员尽量从残骸中打捞物品。
[01:34.32]Nothing of value was found, | 虽然没有发现值钱的东西，
[01:36.48]but the numerous items which were brought to the surface proved to be of great interest. | 但打捞上来的众多物品倒是挺有意思的。
[01:41.75]From a heavy gun that was raised, the captain realized that the ship must have been a cruiser. | 从捞起来的一门重炮来看，船长推断这艘船一定是艘巡洋舰。
[01:48.01]In another chest which contained the belongings of a ship's officer, | 另一只装有船上军官物品的箱子里
[01:52.68]there was an unfinished letter which had been written on March 14th, 1943. | 有一封写于1943年3月14日的未写完的信。
[02:00.01]The captain learnt from the letter that the name of the lost ship was the Karen. | 船长从这封信中得知沉船的名字是“卡伦”号。
[02:05.21]The most valuable find of all was the ship's log book, parts of which it was still possible to read. | 打捞到的东西中最宝贵的是船上的航海日志，其中部分内容仍可辨认。
[02:13.41]From this the captain was able to piece together all the information that had come to light. | 据此，船长能够把所有已经搞清的材料拼凑起来。
[02:19.06]The Karen had been sailing in a convoy to Russia when she was torpedoed by an enemy submarine. | “卡伦”号当时正随船队开往俄国，途中遭敌潜艇鱼雷袭击沉没。
[02:25.63]This was later confirmed by a naval official at the Ministry of Defence after the Elkor had returned home. | 这一点在“埃尔科”号返航后得到国防部一位海军官员的证实。
[02:33.16]All the items that were found were sent to the War Museum. | 打捞到的所有物品均被送往战争博物馆。
